  "id": "twin-cities",
  "intro": "The Twin Cities give you a major airline hub, a working river port fifteen hundred miles from the sea, and the most serious winter of any large American metro — and the last of those shapes the radio. Cold, dry air is exceptionally kind to VHF, the terrain is flat glacial till with nothing to block anything, and in January the band opens up in a way coastal listeners rarely see. The Mississippi starts being navigable here, so there is barge traffic on the marine band through the middle of the city.",
  "introz": "双子城有一个大型航空枢纽、一个距海两千四百公里的内河港，以及全美大城市中最严酷的冬天——而最后这一点决定了这里的无线电。寒冷干燥的空气对 VHF 极为友好，地形是平坦的冰碛地，没有任何遮挡；一月份频段的开放程度是沿海听众很少见到的。密西西比河从这里开始通航，所以市中心就有驳船在海事频段上通话。",
